# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this template is committed.

# Google Sign-In — PUBLIC client ID from Google Cloud Console → Credentials →
# OAuth 2.0 Client IDs. Safe to expose in the bundle.
#
# The client SECRET is deliberately absent: this app uses the Google Identity
# Services ID-token flow, which verifies tokens against Google's published
# public keys. No secret is required on the frontend OR the backend. Never
# commit the downloaded client_secret*.json.
#
# Must match GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID in backend/.env, or tokens fail the `aud` check.
#
# Requires these Authorized JavaScript origins in Google Cloud Console
# (APIs & Services -> Credentials -> your OAuth 2.0 Client ID):
#   http://localhost:5173        (Vite dev)
#   https://cretixone.com        (production storefront)
#   https://www.cretixone.com    (only if www resolves/serves the storefront)
#
# NOTE: no *redirect* URIs are needed — the ID-token flow never redirects.
# NOTE: api.cretixone.com is NOT listed. JavaScript origins are the origins the
#       button is rendered from (the storefront), not the API it posts to.
#
# IMPORTANT: Vite inlines VITE_* vars at BUILD time, and .env is gitignored —
# so this file must exist on whatever machine runs `npm run build`, or the
# client ID compiles to empty and every Google affordance hides itself.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Optional overrides — sensible defaults are built in (see cretixAxios.ts).
# VITE_CRETIX_API_BASE=http://localhost:8000/api/v1
# VITE_UPLOADS_HOST=
